<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="newchar_common.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="newchardescription.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="newchardescription">
    <!-- Tier 4 screen #4 (new-character creator): the OVERVIEW tab (set_description), the last
         step. ROW based, the same vocabulary TRAITS, BIONICS and SKILLS use.

         Two kinds of content share the stage. On the left, the five IDENTITY fields the player can
         still change here (name, gender, height, age, starting location) as an interactive row
         list — before this rework three of the five were unreachable by the cursor and nothing on
         the screen was clickable. On its right, three read-only columns digesting everything the
         earlier steps committed, which is what the six wrapping panes used to do.

         Beside them is the RECORD SEAL: a ring carrying one node per earlier creator step, drawing
         the same runic glyph that step draws in the rail across the top, welded shut by a bead that
         travels the ring once per cycle. A node's glyph colour is its step's state and never
         animates — gold when that step has content, dim when it is empty, red when its budget is
         overspent — so the seal doubles as a validity dashboard. The legend under it names every
         node with its one-line summary, because an unlabelled emblem is decoration.

         Keyboard: UP/DOWN move through the five fields, LEFT/RIGHT change the cursored field's
         value, CONFIRM edits it, and CHANGE_GENDER / CHOOSE_LOCATION / RANDOMIZE_CHAR_DESCRIPTION /
         SAVE_TEMPLATE / REROLL_* / NEXT_TAB / PREV_TAB / QUIT are unchanged. Mouse: a row click
         moves the cursor while the steppers and the edit cell change the character — reading a
         field is not the same gesture as editing one, and two of the five editors are modal.
         See plans/charcreation-overview-seal.md. -->
    <div class="panel nc-panel">
        <div class="nc-steps">
            <div class="nc-step" data-for="t : tabs"
                 data-class-selected="t.selected" data-class-done="t.done">
                <div class="nc-step-icon" data-style-decorator="t.icon_dec"></div>
                <span class="nc-step-label" data-rml="t.name_rml"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="nc-shell">
            <!-- Navigators. Shortcut text comes from the real binding via
                 input_context::get_desc, so it stays correct after a rebind. -->
            <div class="nc-arrow nc-arrow-prev" data-if="has_prev"
                 data-event-click="on_prev()">
                <div class="nc-arrow-glyph">&#60;</div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-key" data-rml="prev_key_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-dest" data-rml="prev_name_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow-spacer" data-if="!has_prev"></div>
            <div class="nc-stage">
                <!-- Meta bar: the points pool left, the finish gate's readiness word right. Both
                     read one nc_finish_gate verdict, so the word here, the STATUS fact below and
                     the NEXT_TAB popup cannot disagree. No balance scale: this step spends nothing. -->
                <div class="nc-rule"></div>
                <div class="nc-meta">
                    <span class="nc-meta-pool" data-rml="points_rml"></span>
                    <span class="nc-meta-budget" data-rml="ready_rml"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="nc-rule"></div>

                <div class="nc-cols">
                    <!-- Wider than the record columns: its values are a name, a gender pair and a
                         location, where theirs are short names and numbers. -->
                    <div class="nc-colwrap nc-ident-col">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <div class="nc-col-sigil" data-style-decorator="ident_sigil_dec"></div>
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="ident_name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="ident_count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <!-- No `item` class on the row, deliberately: theme.rcss's `.item` fill
                             turns a column of rows into one pale slab and flattens every semantic
                             colour in it. Recorded in the bionics plan. -->
                        <div id="nc-col-ident" class="nc-list">
                            <div class="nc-row" data-for="r, ri : ident"
                                 data-class-selected="r.selected"
                                 data-event-click="on_row(ri)">
                                <span class="nc-cell-cursor" data-rml="r.cursor_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-ident-label" data-rml="r.label_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-ident-val" data-rml="r.value_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-step" data-if="r.has_step"
                                      data-class-off="!r.can_dec"
                                      data-event-click="on_dec(ri)">&#8722;</span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-step" data-if="r.has_step"
                                      data-class-off="!r.can_inc"
                                      data-event-click="on_inc(ri)">+</span>
                                <span class="nc-ident-edit"
                                      data-event-click="on_edit(ri)">&#8230;</span>
                            </div>
                            <!-- Scenario and profession: part of the record, not editable HERE, so
                                 they are rows in this column rather than a strip across the top —
                                 and they carry no cursor, which keeps the cursor list exactly the
                                 five fields above. -->
                            <div class="nc-row" data-for="r : background"
                                 data-class-header="r.header">
                                <span class="nc-cell-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-val" data-rml="r.value_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- The three record columns, written out rather than generated: a data-for
                         cannot interleave the dotted rules between its own items, and the shared
                         vocabulary marks a column boundary with .nc-vrule rather than with a solid
                         border (RmlUi has no border-style, so a dotted border renders as nothing). -->
                    <div class="nc-vrule"></div>
                    <div class="nc-colwrap nc-rec-col">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <div class="nc-col-sigil" data-style-decorator="col0.sigil_dec"></div>
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="col0.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="col0.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="nc-list">
                            <div class="nc-row" data-for="r : col0.rows"
                                 data-class-header="r.header">
                                <span class="nc-cell-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-val" data-rml="r.value_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="nc-vrule"></div>
                    <div class="nc-colwrap nc-rec-col">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <div class="nc-col-sigil" data-style-decorator="col1.sigil_dec"></div>
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="col1.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="col1.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="nc-list">
                            <div class="nc-row" data-for="r : col1.rows"
                                 data-class-header="r.header">
                                <span class="nc-cell-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-val" data-rml="r.value_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="nc-vrule"></div>
                    <div class="nc-colwrap nc-rec-col">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <div class="nc-col-sigil" data-style-decorator="col2.sigil_dec"></div>
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="col2.name_rml"></span>
                            <span class="nc-colcount" data-rml="col2.count_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="nc-list">
                            <div class="nc-row" data-for="r : col2.rows"
                                 data-class-header="r.header">
                                <span class="nc-cell-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-cell-val" data-rml="r.value_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="nc-vrule"></div>
                    <!-- Record seal. 13 flex rows of 13 flex cells, so it stays square and aligned
                         at any stage size; C++ writes every cell's socket colour per frame and the
                         cells outside the ring stay fully transparent, which is what makes a square
                         grid read as a ring. Every cell carries both a colour and a decorator —
                         "none" for the ones with no glyph, never an empty string, since
                         `decorator: ;` is a parse error RmlUi logs every frame. Geometry is
                         newchar_seal.h. -->
                    <div class="nc-seal-wrap">
                        <div class="nc-colhead">
                            <span class="nc-colname" data-rml="seal_name_rml"></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="nc-seal">
                            <div class="nc-seal-row" data-for="sr : seal">
                                <div class="nc-seal-cell" data-for="sc : sr.cells"
                                     data-class-node="sc.node"
                                     data-style-background-color="sc.col"
                                     data-style-decorator="sc.dec"></div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="nc-tally">
                            <div class="nc-tally-row" data-for="s : tally">
                                <div class="nc-tally-icon" data-style-decorator="s.dec"></div>
                                <span class="nc-tally-name" data-rml="s.name_rml"></span>
                                <span class="nc-tally-val" data-rml="s.val_rml"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="nc-rule"></div>
                <!-- ":: FIELD NAME" over the detail panel, as on every other step. -->
                <div class="nc-selname" data-rml="sel_name_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-info-panel">
                    <!-- Art slot: the character portrait, where every other preview-bearing step
                         puts it. The absolutely positioned top-right box this screen used to have
                         dates from the era when the avatar was a GPU sprite the panels had to
                         dodge. -->
                    <div class="nc-info-art" data-if="has_portrait"
                         data-style-decorator="portrait_dec"></div>
                    <div class="nc-info-facts">
                        <div class="nc-fact" data-for="f : facts">
                            <div class="nc-fact-label" data-rml="f.label_rml"></div>
                            <div class="nc-fact-value" data-rml="f.value_rml"></div>
                            <div class="nc-fact-sub" data-rml="f.sub_rml"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Prose in a .nc-info-blurb CHILD: .nc-info-desc is `display: flex`, and a
                         bare text node in a flex container gets no inline context and renders
                         nothing. See plans/charcreation-stats-cards.md. -->
                    <div class="nc-info-desc">
                        <div class="nc-info-blurb" data-rml="desc_rml"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="nc-hint" data-rml="hint_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow nc-arrow-next" data-if="has_next"
                 data-event-click="on_next()">
                <div class="nc-arrow-glyph">&#62;</div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-key" data-rml="next_key_rml"></div>
                <div class="nc-arrow-dest" data-rml="next_name_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="nc-arrow-spacer" data-if="!has_next"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="nc-exit" data-rml="exit_rml"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="crt-overlay" class="crt"></div>
</body>
</rml>
